$ =========================================================================
$ airplane_aero.bdf — Generic regional jet: wing + empennage
$ Structural skeleton + VLM aerodynamic panels (no aero corrections)
$
$ Coordinate system: X = freestream (forward), Y = starboard, Z = up
$ Units: SI (m, N, kg, Pa)
$
$ Full-span model (SYMXZ=0): both wing halves and both HTP halves modelled
$ explicitly; no mirror image added by the VLM solver.
$ VTP lies in the XZ plane (y=0) and is modelled as a single CAERO1.
$
$ Aircraft geometry summary:
$   Wing:  span 24 m (12 m each side), root chord 4.0 m, tip chord 1.6 m
$          root LE at (10, 0, 0), stbd tip LE at (14, 12, 0) — 18 deg LE sweep
$   HTP:   span 10 m (5 m each side), root chord 2.0 m, tip chord 1.0 m
$          root LE at (30, 0, 0), stbd tip LE at (33,  5, 0) — 31 deg LE sweep
$   VTP:   height 5 m, root chord 4.0 m, tip chord 2.0 m
$          root LE at (29, 0, 0), tip LE at (32.5, 0, 5) — 35 deg LE sweep
$ =========================================================================
$
SOL 101
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE = Airplane 1g Static Load
  SPC   = 1
  LOAD  = 10
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
  SPCFORCE     = ALL
  OLOAD        = ALL
  FORCE        = ALL
  STRESS       = ALL
$
BEGIN BULK
$
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------- MATERIAL
$ Aluminium alloy (2024-T3 representative)
$ E=70 GPa, G=26.9 GPa, nu=0.3, rho=2700 kg/m^3
MAT1, 1, 7.0e10, 2.69e10, 0.3, 2700.0
$
$ ---------------------------------------------------------------- PROPERTIES
$ PID 1 — Fuselage equivalent beam (simplified representative section)
$ A=0.15 m^2, I1=0.30 m^4 (vertical bending), I2=0.30 m^4 (lateral), J=0.50 m^4
PBAR, 1, 1, 0.15, 0.30, 0.30, 0.50
$
$ PID 2 — Wing structural box
$ A=0.04 m^2, I1=0.08 m^4 (flapwise), I2=0.004 m^4 (chordwise), J=0.030 m^4
PBAR, 2, 1, 0.04, 0.08, 0.004, 0.030
$
$ PID 3 — Empennage box (HTP and VTP share property for simplicity)
$ A=0.02 m^2, I1=0.020 m^4, I2=0.001 m^4, J=0.008 m^4
PBAR, 3, 1, 0.02, 0.020, 0.001, 0.008
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------------- NODES
$ Fuselage spine (along X-axis, y=0, z=0)
$ GID, CP, X, Y, Z
GRID, 1, , 0.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID, 2, , 6.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID, 3, , 12.0, 0.0, 0.0
GRID, 4, , 21.0, 0.0, 0.0
GRID, 5, , 30.0, 0.0, 0.0
$
$ Wing elastic axis — starboard (y > 0)
GRID, 11, , 12.0,  4.0, 0.0
GRID, 12, , 12.0,  8.0, 0.0
GRID, 13, , 12.0, 12.0, 0.0
$
$ Wing elastic axis — port (y < 0, mirror of starboard)
GRID, 111, , 12.0,  -4.0, 0.0
GRID, 112, , 12.0,  -8.0, 0.0
GRID, 113, , 12.0, -12.0, 0.0
$
$ HTP elastic axis — starboard
GRID, 21, , 30.6, 2.5, 0.0
GRID, 22, , 31.2, 5.0, 0.0
$
$ HTP elastic axis — port
GRID, 121, , 30.6, -2.5, 0.0
GRID, 122, , 31.2, -5.0, 0.0
$
$ VTP elastic axis (vertical, spans upward in Z from tail attach)
GRID, 31, , 30.6, 0.0, 2.5
GRID, 32, , 31.2, 0.0, 5.0
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------ ELEMENTS
$ Fuselage CBAR elements — orientation vec (0,1,0): elem-y = global Y
CBAR, 1, 1, 1, 2, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 2, 1, 2, 3, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 3, 1, 3, 4, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 4, 1, 4, 5, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
$
$ Wing CBAR elements — starboard; orientation vec (1,0,0): elem-y = global X
$ I1 = flapwise (bending about chord axis), I2 = chordwise (in-plane)
CBAR, 11, 2, 3,   11, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 12, 2, 11,  12, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 13, 2, 12,  13, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$
$ Wing CBAR elements — port (mirror)
CBAR, 111, 2, 3,   111, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 112, 2, 111, 112, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 113, 2, 112, 113, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$
$ HTP CBAR elements — starboard
CBAR, 21, 3, 5,  21, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 22, 3, 21, 22, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$
$ HTP CBAR elements — port
CBAR, 121, 3, 5,   121, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
CBAR, 122, 3, 121, 122, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$
$ VTP CBAR elements — orientation vec (0,1,0): elem-y = global Y (sidewise)
$ I1 = lateral bending (fin flaps sideways), I2 = chordwise bending
CBAR, 31, 3, 5,  31, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 32, 3, 31, 32, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------- CONSTRAINTS
$ Fix all 6 DOFs at forward reference node (wind tunnel / ground mount)
SPC1, 1, 123456, 1
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------------- LOADS
$ 1g body acceleration, -Z direction
GRAV, 10, 0, 9.81, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0
$
$ ============================================================== AERODYNAMICS
$ Reference geometry (full-span model)
$ CREF = 3.0 m (wing mean aerodynamic chord)
$ BREF = 24.0 m (full span = 2 x 12 m semi-span)
$ SREF = 67.2 m^2 (full wing ref area = 2 x 0.5*(4.0+1.6)*12)
$ SYMXZ=0: full-span model, no mirror image
AEROS, 0, 0, 3.0, 24.0, 67.2, 0, 0
$
$ Aerodynamic panel property (Phase A stub — no fuselage body support)
PAERO1, 10
$
$ Chordwise resolution: NCHORD = 8 on every surface.
$   Steady VLM lift converges at NCHORD=1, but chordwise loading and pitching
$   moment do not — CM is ~50% off at NCHORD=2 and only settles by NCHORD~8
$   (verified by chordwise convergence study). Minimum recommended = 4; 8 used
$   here for converged moments. Cosine chordwise spacing (LCHORD + AEFACT)
$   would reach the same accuracy with fewer boxes — NASA SP-405. Phase D (DLM)
$   will need more (Rodden/MSC).
$
$ Spanwise resolution: NSPAN sized so each box aspect ratio (spanwise edge /
$   streamwise edge) is near 1.0 — target ~1, acceptable band 0.5-2.0. High-AR
$   boxes degrade the VLM induced-downwash kernel and bias the loading; keeping
$   AR ~ O(1) is standard VLM/DLM practice (NASA SP-405; Rodden/MSC). With
$   NCHORD=8 and these chords the chordwise box length is short, so NSPAN must
$   be correspondingly high to match it:
$     Wing  NSPAN=38 -> box AR 0.64-1.63 (mean 0.99), 304 boxes/half
$     HTP   NSPAN=31 -> box AR 0.70-1.47 (mean 1.00), 248 boxes/half
$     VTP   NSPAN=16 -> box AR 0.67-1.46 (mean 0.97), 128 boxes
$   Total 1232 boxes (was 192). Uniform spacing; AR varies root->tip with taper
$   (root box has widest chord -> lowest AR, tip narrowest -> highest AR).
$
$ ---- Wing starboard: 38 spanwise x 8 chordwise = 304 boxes
$ P1 = root LE (10.0,   0.0, 0.0), X12 = 4.0 m (root chord)
$ P4 = tip  LE (14.0,  12.0, 0.0), X43 = 1.6 m (tip  chord)
CAERO1, 1000, 10, 0, 38, 8, 0, 0, 1
+, 10.0, 0.0, 0.0, 4.0, 14.0, 12.0, 0.0, 1.6
$
$ ---- Wing port: 38 spanwise x 8 chordwise = 304 boxes
$ P1 = root LE (10.0,   0.0, 0.0), X12 = 4.0 m
$ P4 = tip  LE (14.0, -12.0, 0.0), X43 = 1.6 m  (tip at negative Y)
CAERO1, 2000, 10, 0, 38, 8, 0, 0, 1
+, 10.0, 0.0, 0.0, 4.0, 14.0, -12.0, 0.0, 1.6
$
$ ---- HTP starboard: 31 spanwise x 8 chordwise = 248 boxes
$ P1 = root LE (30.0, 0.0, 0.0), X12 = 2.0 m
$ P4 = tip  LE (33.0, 5.0, 0.0), X43 = 1.0 m
CAERO1, 3000, 10, 0, 31, 8, 0, 0, 1
+, 30.0, 0.0, 0.0, 2.0, 33.0, 5.0, 0.0, 1.0
$
$ ---- HTP port: 31 spanwise x 8 chordwise = 248 boxes
$ P1 = root LE (30.0,  0.0, 0.0), X12 = 2.0 m
$ P4 = tip  LE (33.0, -5.0, 0.0), X43 = 1.0 m
CAERO1, 4000, 10, 0, 31, 8, 0, 0, 1
+, 30.0, 0.0, 0.0, 2.0, 33.0, -5.0, 0.0, 1.0
$
$ ---- VTP (full surface; "span" is Z from z=0 to z=5): 16 x 8 = 128 boxes
$ Lies in the XZ plane (y=0); no symmetry duplication with SYMXZ=0.
$ P1 = root LE (29.0, 0.0, 0.0), X12 = 4.0 m
$ P4 = tip  LE (32.5, 0.0, 5.0), X43 = 2.0 m
CAERO1, 5000, 10, 0, 16, 8, 0, 0, 1
+, 29.0, 0.0, 0.0, 4.0, 32.5, 0.0, 5.0, 2.0
$
ENDDATA
